<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SPEC.md 4.4a - Marked for Death's damage over time.

  History, because this def has been wrong twice:

  1. First attempt used vanilla DamageDefOf.Deterioration - the ITEM decay type, which does
     nothing at all to a pawn. No damage appeared in playtest.
  2. Second attempt parented this to Scratch. That worked, but Scratch makes CUTS, and once the
     damage was spread across the whole body the victim had a dozen small open wounds at once.
     RimWorld sums bleed rate across wounds, so everything marked died of blood loss - deadlier
     than the concentrated version it was meant to soften.

  Now parented to Blunt, whose injuries are crushes and bruises rather than cuts. It still
  damages properly and is still reduced by armour - which pairs with the mark's armour penalty -
  but it does not open a dozen bleeding wounds. A wasting curse should not make someone bleed.

  The application count is also capped in HediffComp_DamageOverTime, so total damage is bounded.
-->
<Defs>

  <DamageDef ParentName="BluntBase">
    <defName>Dovahkiin_SoulWither</defName>
    <label>withering</label>
    <deathMessage>{0} has withered away under the Thu'um.</deathMessage>
  </DamageDef>

  <!--
    A DRAGON'S FROST BREATH. SPEC.md 4.6.

    ⚠ WHY THIS EXISTS INSTEAD OF USING VANILLA Frostbite DIRECTLY.

    Vanilla's Frostbite has NO armorCategory at all, and Verse.ArmorUtility.GetPostArmorDamage
    opens with "if (damageDef.armorCategory == null) return amount;" - so Frostbite IGNORES EVERY
    KIND OF ARMOUR COMPLETELY. Not sharp, not blunt, not heat, and armour penetration means
    nothing against it.

    That is fine for the Dovahkiin's own Frost Breath, which the player aims at raiders. It is NOT
    fine for a dragon breathing at the player: a colonist in cataphract plate under a three-word
    Dragon Aspect would take exactly what a naked one takes. The user is already asking why Dragon
    Aspect feels thin against dragon FIRE - shipping a frost breath that ignores armour outright
    would be strictly worse than the thing they complained about.

    So this is Frostbite's behaviour - same worker, same frostbite hediff - with an armorCategory
    added so protection means something. HEAT is the right category rather than a compromise: it
    is what RimWorld uses for temperature damage, and it makes Dragon Aspect's fire resistance
    cover a dragon's breath of EITHER element, which is what "dragon aspect" ought to mean.

    ⚠ THE DOVAHKIIN'S OWN FROST BREATH IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED and still uses vanilla Frostbite.
    Her shout is a different thing pointed the other way, and it is signed off.
  -->
  <DamageDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonFrost</defName>
    <label>dragon frost</label>
    <workerClass>DamageWorker_Frostbite</workerClass>
    <externalViolence>true</externalViolence>
    <deathMessage>{0} has been frozen solid by a dragon's breath.</deathMessage>
    <hediff>Frostbite</hediff>
    <harmAllLayersUntilOutside>true</harmAllLayersUntilOutside>
    <armorCategory>Heat</armorCategory>
    <impactSoundType>Slice</impactSoundType>
  </DamageDef>

</Defs>
